{"rev":13,"ts":"2026-10-29T22:04:22.805038379+00:00","fields":{"__previous_part_content__":"Previous Part: [04](04-revision-bound-approval.md) | Next Part: [06](06-discoverable-mcp-surface.md)\n\n# 05 — Lifecycle, handoff, results, and controlled reopen\n\n## Outcome\n\nImplement pause/resume, session handoff, cancel, complete, review-results/add\nwaypoints, and reopening of the most recently durably completed waypoint with\nCAS protection and Ticket-authoritative controlled reopen.\n\n## Non-goal\n\nDo not select the final execution-order waypoint, erase result history,\nsilently map cancellation to blocked, or rewrite a terminal Ticket directly.\n\n## Inputs and implementation boundary\n\nUse W1-W4. Completion events are append-only and sequence-ordered; reopening\npreserves results, invalidates approval, and makes descendants non-executable\nuntil revised approval. A Ticket-backed operation calls a legal Ticket\ntransition or returns `ticket_transition_rejected`.\n\nThe selected completed event must still be the current completion of a\ncompleted waypoint. Reopen moves that waypoint to planned; for Ticket-backed\nwork the Ticket domain performs an explicit audited done-to-ready reopen\noperation. This work includes adding that supported operation if the current\nTicket schema lacks it; rejection is not the successful happy path.\nAlready reopened events are not eligible. Existing results remain immutable\nhistorical observations, and dependent completion evidence is marked stale\nfor the revised route rather than silently considered current.\n\nPersist a cross-store operation journal with Ticket/Mission preconditions.\nDuring interrupted reopen, neither Mission nor dependents are executable.\nRetry finishes the recorded operation or reports the precise persisted subset;\nnever roll back by erasing Ticket history. Include these failure windows in\ntests, not only competing Mission revisions.\n\n## Expected post-state and validation\n\nConcurrent reopen attempts select exactly one latest completion event using\nCAS; a later completion wins regardless of waypoint order. Result history\nsurvives reopening/restart, descendants require reapproval, and controlled\nTicket reopen is read back from Ticket authority.\n\nFuture targets: `cd workflow-tools && cargo test -p mission -p ticket-api`;\ninclude competing CAS, out-of-order completion, descendant, result-history,\ncancel, handoff, and rejected-Ticket-transition cases.\n\n## Checkpoint\n\nCommit lifecycle behavior plus cross-store tests after passing.\n\n","__previous_part_id__":"9923cbc3-6959-49d9-a40b-0356b544ad98","component":"mission.native-planning.lifecycle-reopen","depends_on":["1d6816b5-92d6-4a08-858a-94df3a05b3f4"],"linked":["f77e35d8-8d74-4160-9ed0-85bf32c62a97"],"parts":[{"id":"34e4bd94-9bac-4d1f-bf79-eea1e612da69","kind":"requirements","path":"parts/requirements.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:41.670974470Z"},{"id":"9923cbc3-6959-49d9-a40b-0356b544ad98","kind":"design","path":"parts/design.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:41.738271227Z"},{"id":"b54f28b3-43ff-4774-bb27-a209e0ecc365","kind":"examples","path":"parts/examples.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:41.809250051Z"},{"id":"b1596949-249d-456e-afaa-1317d8fad925","kind":"acceptance_criteria","path":"parts/acceptance-criteria.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:41.880570197Z"},{"id":"57f8abe8-f3fd-4317-8e5d-97dcb5be4ab5","kind":"validation","path":"parts/validation.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:41.949958791Z"},{"id":"e5c1fb22-bcfc-401d-97fc-ad619b3ece10","kind":"notes","path":"parts/notes.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:42.022219558Z"},{"id":"09c627f7-3804-4845-9d36-02f23de2939c","kind":"objective","path":"parts/objective.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T22:00:44.001988753Z"}],"priority":"high","refs":[{"kind":"spec","urn":"ce://default/spec/164e9acd-9781-4455-b835-f7121a275eef","note":"Owning native pla